      "split": "holdout",
      "category": "factual",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "question": "What values can a diagnosis fix_type take?",
      "history": [],
      "historyStatuses": [],
      "answer": "Evidence: `prash/connectors/base.py:L46-L72`. - [implemented] `Diagnosis` requires `problem_summary` (10–500 chars), `root_cause` and `fix_description` (20–2000 chars each), `fix_type`, `confidence` between 0 and 1, and a `category`. [1] Reversible: True. - Class: `EditConfigMapAction` at `prash/actions/edit_config.py:L77-L115`; spec at `prash/actions/edit_config.py:L79-L86`. - Registered in the CLI dispatcher: yes. - Contract methods defined in the class: execute, verify. - Summary (from the spec): Merge-patch keys into an existing ConfigMap - Approval hint (from the spec): Always prompts, even in bypass mode -- a bad config value can take a running service down as surely as a bad rollback. - Capabilities: `('get_configmap', 'update_configmap')`. [2] Evidence: `prash/cli.py:L585-L608`. - [implemented] When the diagnosis returns a ranked options menu, non-interactive runs report the menu and take no action; interactive runs let the operator pick, and the pick still goes through risk tiers, the circuit breaker and the audit log. [3]",
