      "split": "holdout",
      "category": "security",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "question": "Which risk tier and permission mode does /api/chat/execute record in the audit log?",
      "history": [],
      "historyStatuses": [],
      "answer": "Values are never echoed to the console or audit log — only key names are. - Capabilities: `('get_secret_keys', 'update_secret')`. - Risk tier: approval. [1] Evidence: `tests/test_desktop_api.py:L724-L749`. - [implemented] The endpoint's own audit entry is written with risk tier SAFE and mode ASK whatever the real action was. [2] Evidence: `prash/server.py:L2705-L2726`. - [implemented] After the call the handler appends an audit entry with risk tier SAFE and mode ASK regardless of the action's real tier. [5]",
      "citations": [
